# 04 — Compatibility and versioning

<!-- GEN: Why: clients already installed or deployed keep calling the old shape; breaking them is the costliest API mistake. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->

<!-- GEN: Rule AP6. Link the contract list and bump rules of git-workflow instead of restating them. -->

Prefer adding over modifying. Any observable behavior (error text, ordering, defaults, extra fields, timing) may already be relied on by a client (Hyrum's Law): a change to it is checked against the clients below before it is called compatible.

| Change | Compatible? | How to do it |
|---|---|---|
| Add an optional field or endpoint | Yes | Add to the contract, clients ignore unknown fields |
| Add a required request field | No | {{required_field_path}} |
| Rename or remove a field | No | {{rename_path}} |
| Change a field's meaning or type | No | {{meaning_path}} |
| Remove an endpoint | No | {{remove_path}} |

Versioning: {{versioning_rule}} · Deprecation: {{deprecation_rule}}

One live version per API (One-Version Rule): extend it instead of forking a parallel version; a new version, when unavoidable, comes with the retirement date of the old one.

Clients that must keep working: {{supported_clients}}

